-- title:
--   Unique supersingular prime with trivial residue extension
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ let $K$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the image under coefficientwise extension $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, and $K_1$ the corresponding subfield attached to $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, with $K_1 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, and $A$ acts compatibly on $K$ and $K_1$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ and $j_1 \in K_1$ be the nonzero elements whose Laurent expansions are the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K,j)$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and similarly $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K_1,j_1) \subseteq K_1$, and let $\iota_F$ be an $A$-algebra map between them compatible with the inclusions of Laurent series. Let $y$ be a prime of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K,j)$ containing $\varpi$ and supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K,j)$ to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $p$-torsion point. Then: any prime $y'$ of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K,j)$ with the same contraction along $\iota_F$ as $y$ equals $y$; and every $s \in A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K,j)$ satisfies $s - \iota_F(r) \in y$ for some $r \in A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K_1,j_1)$.
--
--   This is the statement that the degree-$(p-1)$ covering $X_1(Mp) \to X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$ given by the diamond operators at $p$ is totally ramified, with trivial residue extension, above each supersingular point of the characteristic-$p$ fibre, formulated for the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model over $A$. It feeds the analysis of supersingular points on these integral models, in particular the compatibility with the diamond automorphisms and the construction of the associated stalk data.
